 CO4.2  UNIX INODE STRUCTURE AND ADDRESSING REACH
==============================================================================
   Block size 4096 B, pointer 4 B -> 1024 pointers per indirect block

   Pointer tier              Blocks reachable             Bytes  Reads to fetch
   10 direct                               10             40 KB               1
   1 single indirect                    1,024          4.000 MB               2
   1 double indirect                1,048,576          4.000 GB               3
   1 triple indirect            1,073,741,824          4.000 TB               4
   MAXIMUM FILE SIZE            1,074,791,434          4.004 TB

   The asymmetry is the whole point of the design: 99.99% of files in
   a real system fit inside the 10 direct pointers and cost exactly
   one disk read, while the rare huge file is still addressable, at a
   worst case of 4 reads per block.

