 CO4.2  bmap() - which pointer tier serves a given logical block?
==============================================================================
     Logical block       File offset                  Tier   Disk reads
                 0              0 KB                direct            1
                 9             36 KB                direct            1
                10             40 KB       single indirect            2
             1,033           4.04 MB       single indirect            2
             1,034           4.04 MB       double indirect            3
         1,049,610           4.00 GB       triple indirect            4
         1,049,700           4.00 GB       triple indirect            4
        13,107,199          50.00 GB       triple indirect            4

==============================================================================
 CO4.2  METADATA COST OF A 50 GB VM DISK IMAGE (guest-win11.vmdk)
==============================================================================
   named.conf (2 KB)           data            1 blocks   indirect        0 blocks   overhead  0.000%
   nginx-access.log (80 MB)    data       20,480 blocks   indirect       21 blocks   overhead  0.103%
   guest-ubuntu.img (8 GB)     data    2,097,152 blocks   indirect    2,051 blocks   overhead  0.098%
   guest-win11.vmdk (50 GB)    data   13,107,200 blocks   indirect   12,814 blocks   overhead  0.098%

   A 50 GB image needs 12,814 indirect blocks -- 50 MB of pure pointer
   metadata that must itself be cached, and up to 4 disk reads to
   reach one data block on a cold cache. This is precisely why ext4
   replaced the indirect chain with extents for large files: a single
   12-byte extent descriptor covers up to 128 MB contiguously.

